1. AXE — target-size / empty-table-header / no other violation
`node audit.js` ran axe twice per page (WCAG-tag run, and a `runOnly: {type:
'rule', values:['target-size','empty-table-header']}` forced run) across
{BK2,MASTER} × {1300,390} × {light,dark}, all with every `<details>` open
and the pin-check ticked:
  BK2_1300_light: wcag=[] forced=[]
  BK2_1300_dark:  wcag=[] forced=[]
  BK2_390_light:  wcag=[] forced=[]
  BK2_390_dark:   wcag=[] forced=[]
  MASTER_1300_light: wcag=[] forced=['empty-table-header']
  MASTER_1300_dark:  wcag=[] forced=['empty-table-header']
  MASTER_390_light:  wcag=[] forced=['empty-table-header']
  MASTER_390_dark:   wcag=[] forced=['empty-table-header']
Zero target-size, zero empty-table-header on BK2 in all 4 combinations; the
full WCAG-tag axe run adds zero violations on BK2 in any combination (no
regression introduced). empty-table-header cleanly fixed vs MASTER (which
hits it in all 4).
OBSERVATION on the task brief's premise: MASTER did NOT actually get a
`target-size` axe hit in this real render — I dumped axe's `passes` array
for `target-size` on MASTER (`node audit3.js` / `audit4.js`) and every small
control (14.875×14.875 row-toggle, 21.25px-tall Clear button) PASSES via
axe's `target-offset` escape hatch (≥24px clearance to the nearest
neighbour target satisfies WCAG 2.5.8's spacing exception even when the
target itself is undersized) — e.g. `#major-expenses-bulk-pin-clear` passes
target-size only via the `target-offset` `any` check, not the `target-size`
check itself. So "master had both rule hits" in my brief was inaccurate for
target-size specifically (accurate for empty-table-header). This doesn't
change the verdict: BK2's controls now pass on genuine size (measured
25.5×25.5 / 34px-tall, both ≥24px) rather than relying on the spacing
exception — a strictly more robust result — and node measurements
(`node inspect.js`) confirm the real pixel sizes:
  MASTER: apply 50.6×21.25 (disabled), clear 47.97×21.25, toggle 14.875×14.875
  BK2:    apply 64.69×34 (disabled), clear 61.59×34, toggle 25.5×25.5
Apply enabled-state re-measured (`node apply_enabled.js`, real
`selectOption` + `check()`, opacity:1, disabled:false): 64.69×34 sized
identically to the disabled-state box.

2. Points 3/9 — toggle accessible name, aria-expanded, Tab order, focus ring
`node toggle_check.js` (real click, real `Enter`, real `Space`, on the live
:8213 page, 1300 light/dark and 390 light):
  accName (aria-label) = "Details for Amazon"; SVG carries aria-hidden="true"
    (icon is decorative, name comes from the button's own aria-label — a
    screen reader announces "Details for Amazon, button, collapsed/expanded").
  beforeExpanded=false → click → afterExpanded=true → detailVisible=true
    (aria-controls target genuinely toggled visible, not just the ARIA
    attribute) → Enter → false → Space → true. Both keyboard activation
    paths work identically to mouse click; aria-expanded genuinely tracks
    state in all three cases; consistent across all three viewport/theme
    combinations run.
Tab order: `node tab_to_toggle.js` — real sequential Tab from
`#major-expenses-search`, landed on a `.major-expense-row-toggle` (Amazon,
aria-expanded="false") at step 70, immediately preceded by the checkbox
list / pin buttons / bulk-pin toolbar in DOM order — i.e. reachable, and in
document order (no tabindex was touched by the diff — `git diff` confirms
zero tabindex/DOM-reorder changes, so relative order is unchanged by
construction; the walk confirms reachability empirically).
Focus ring (real Tab-reachable button, then `.focus()` used only to hold
state for the screenshot): computed style is UA-default (`outline: rgb(16,
16, 16) auto 1px`, unaffected by the BK1 `:focus-visible` rule list, which
does not include `.major-expense-row-toggle`, and unaffected by the BK1
`input/select/textarea:focus` box-shadow rule — buttons are out of both).
Pixel-sampled from real Playwright screenshots (`node ring_shot.js` +
PIL/WCAG-formula contrast):
  BK2 light: ring rgb(16,16,16) vs bg rgb(255,255,255) → 19.03:1  PASS
  BK2 dark:  ring rgb(68,64,60) vs bg rgb(41,37,36)     → 1.48:1  FAILS 3:1
FAIL ATTRIBUTION (constitution point 9 / WCAG 1.4.11): dark-mode focus ring
on `.major-expense-row-toggle` is real and measured, but PRE-EXISTING —
`node ring_shot_master.js` against MASTER on :8223 (same real click/focus/
screenshot method, same button, same theme) measures the IDENTICAL ring
colour and background (`rgb(68,64,60)` vs `rgb(41,37,36)` → 1.48:1) on the
14.875×14.875 master button. BK2's diff never touches any `:focus` or
`:focus-visible` selector (confirmed above; the only focus-ring change in
this worktree is BK1's `styles.css`, scoped to input/select/textarea, and
is foreign/already-accepted per the task brief). This is scored per the
constitution's diff-attribution rule as an OBSERVATION with provenance, not
a BK2 FAIL — it is a pre-existing sitewide gap (button focus rings are not
covered by BK1's accent-token fix) worth flagging for a future task.

3. Point 2 — "Details" header sr-only, column count unchanged
`node misc_check.js` (real render, both themes/viewports):
  BK2 header <th> textContent = "Details"; a clone with `.sr-only` removed
    has textContent = "" (i.e., zero visible text, full accessible name) —
    confirmed again via `node axe_name_check.js`: {"text":"Details",
    "visibleText":""}.
  span computed style: position:absolute, width:1px, height:1px,
    overflow:hidden, clip:rect(0px,0px,0px,0px) — genuinely visually hidden,
    not display:none (so it stays in the accessibility tree).
  Column counts identical BK2 vs MASTER: headerCellCount=168,
    firstBodyRowCellCount=4, in every combination tested — the header
    addition does not change the table's structural column count.

4. Points 7/12 — Apply/Clear contrast at the new size, both themes
Colours are unchanged by the diff (only padding/font-size classes
changed); computed styles + WCAG contrast formula (relative luminance):
  Apply, both themes: white rgb(255,255,255) on warning-strong
    rgb(146,64,14) → 7.09:1 (enabled state re-verified separately at
    opacity:1 — same 7.09:1; the toolbar's default disabled state doesn't
    weaken this since disabled controls are exempt from 1.4.3/1.4.11 in any
    case).
  Clear light: gray-700 rgb(68,64,60) on gray-200 rgb(231,229,228) → 8.18:1
  Clear dark:  gray-100 rgb(245,245,244) on gray-600 rgb(87,83,78) → 6.99:1
All ≥ 4.5:1 (text is 14.875px/400-weight — not "large text" by WCAG's
18.66px/14pt-bold threshold, so the strict 4.5:1 applies and is cleared
with margin).

5. Reflow at 390 / toggle column width
`node misc_check.js`, 390×844, both themes:
  docScrollW === docClientW (390===390); tableScrollW === tableClientW
  (322===322) — no horizontal overflow from the enlarged toggles at either
   viewport (1300: 1300/1300, 1212/1212 also equal).
Column width: header `<th class="w-6">` is unchanged in the diff (no class
edit — confirmed above). The RENDERED th width did grow (25.5px on MASTER
→ 34px on BK2) because the table uses `table-layout: auto` and the column
width is driven by its widest cell content, which is now the 25.5×25.5
toggle button (was a bare 14.875px icon) — this is the intended, in-scope
consequence of enlarging the toggle per the task, not an unrequested class
change to the header; it does not cause overflow (see scrollWidth checks
above) and is reported as an OBSERVATION, not a defect.

