OBSERVATIONS (non-blocking, for the backlog)
- Constitution point 9 / WCAG 1.4.11: `.major-expense-row-toggle` (and by
  extension any other bare `<button>` on the page not in BK1's
  `:focus-visible` selector list) has a 1.48:1 dark-mode focus ring —
  invisible-in-practice. PRE-EXISTING (measured byte-identical on master),
  out of BK2's scope, but a good BK3-class candidate: extend BK1's
  `:focus-visible` selector list (or add a generic `button:focus-visible`
  rule) to cover it.
- The task brief's claim that MASTER hits axe `target-size` was not borne
  out by a real axe run — MASTER passes via the `target-offset` spacing
  exception. Worth correcting in future BK-series briefs; does not affect
  this verdict since BK2's fix is still a genuine, measured size increase
  past the 24px threshold on its own merits.
- Rendered toggle-column `<th>` width grew from 25.5px to 34px as a
  side-effect of `table-layout: auto` sizing to the larger button; no
  overflow resulted, but if a future task tightens columns further this is
  the layout mechanism to be aware of.

